  "scarica": "Download",
  "ultimoAggiornamento": "Last updated: {p0}",
  "breveTuoiDatiRestano": "In short: your data stays on the phone. The app has no server, account or ads, and doesn't sell or share your data. It only leaves the phone in the cases described below, almost all chosen by you.",
  "datiInserisciTu": "Data you enter",
  "nomeDataNascitaSesso": "Name, date of birth, sex, height, weight and measurements, profile photo, goal and race, typical week, equipment, feedback after workouts (effort, completed, pain), reps and kg of strength sets, climbing routes, problems, grades and workouts, lengths, times and other session data written by hand, hand-written plans and sessions imported from CSV files. They're used to prepare the plan and show progress.",
  "datiLettiHealthConnect": "Data read from Health Connect (read-only)",
  "tuoPermessoAppLegge": "With your permission the app reads workout sessions from Health Connect (type, title, start and end) and, within the time of each session, heart rate, distance, calories, steps and speed. It also reads resting HR, heart rate variability (HRV) and sleep to assess recovery, and history older than 30 days if you allow it. This is the data written by Garmin Connect, Freeletics and the other apps connected to Health Connect. The app doesn't write, change or delete anything in Health Connect.",
  "percorsiGpsDelleSessioni": "GPS routes of sessions",
  "seAppHaRegistrato": "If the app that recorded a run or a ride also saved the route in Health Connect, Avidididadi reads it only with your permission: for the single session (Health Connect asks you) or for all of them, if you choose \"Always allow\" in the Health Connect settings. You can also add a route yourself by loading a GPX file (for example exported from Garmin Connect). A copy of the route stays in the app to show the map. The routes to follow that you add to \"My routes\" (GPX files of races, loops, friends) stay only on the phone and in the backup; they don't go to the assistant.",
  "posizioneDuranteAllenamento": "Location during the workout",
  "soloCorsaCamminataBici": "Only for running, walking and cycling (and for another activity if you choose to record the route), and only while workout mode is open, the app uses precise location (GPS and the Google Play location service on the phone) to record route, distance and pace. While recording it shows a persistent notification and keeps going even with the screen off; when you close the workout the GPS turns off. The app doesn't use location at any other time and doesn't collect it in the background. The route is saved only on the phone: it doesn't go to Health Connect, it doesn't go to the assistant and it isn't sent to anyone, unless you turn on sending to intervals.icu or save it to a GPX file. While you train, a copy of the session in progress (route included) stays on the phone so it can be resumed if the app closes; it's deleted when you finish.",
  "sensoriBluetoothBattitoBici": "Bluetooth sensors (heart rate and bike)",
  "soloSeScegliTu": "Only if you choose to, during workout mode or from the \"My sensors\" page in Profile, the app connects via Bluetooth to a chest strap, a watch that broadcasts heart rate or bike sensors (trainer, power, speed and cadence), to show them while you train. When that page is closed or the workout is over, it disconnects. At the end of the session it saves in the session the average and maximum heart rate, average power and cadence and, for the charts, one value per second of heart rate, power, cadence and speed: all on the phone. The Bluetooth name and address of the sensors (and the wheel circumference) stay on the phone to reconnect next time: you delete them with \"Forget\". The \"Nearby devices\" permission is only used to find the sensor, not to know where you are.",
  "mappe": "Maps",
  "disegnareMappaAppScarica": "To draw the map the app downloads the tiles of the area shown: from OpenFreeMap (tiles.openfreemap.org, data © OpenStreetMap) for the Pulse and Streets maps, and from Esri (server.arcgisonline.com) only if you choose the Satellite view. As with any website, those services receive the phone's IP address and which tiles are requested, so they can tell which area you're looking at. The route, times and other workout data are not sent: the line is drawn on the phone. For routes to follow, the app downloads in advance the tiles of the strip around the track, to see them offline: OpenFreeMap receives those tiles, and therefore the area of the route. They stay in the app's memory until you remove the map or the route.",
  "intervalsIcuFacoltativo": "intervals.icu (optional)",
  "seColleghiIntervalsIcu": "If you connect intervals.icu with your API key, the app downloads from there your running, cycling and swimming activities (name, times, distance, heart rate, speed, altitude, power, GPS route) and your bike and running FTP, for the power zones. intervals.icu receives them from your watch (Garmin, Polar, Suunto…) because you connected it, under its own privacy terms. The key stays encrypted on the phone. Only if you turn on \"Send plan and sessions to intervals.icu\" does the app write to your intervals.icu calendar the running, cycling and swimming sessions of the next 14 days (date, sport, name, duration, steps with heart rate, power or pace zones): no name, photo, measurements, feedback or strength. Turning it off removes the future sessions sent by the app. With this sending on, every session you record with the app (strength included) goes to your account by itself as soon as it's finished; off, only if you tap \"Send to intervals.icu\" on that session. What's sent: time, sport, name, duration, distance, average and maximum heart rate and, if there is one, the GPS route. In the same way \"Save GPX\" creates a file with the route where you choose. Downloaded activities stay on the phone and go into the backup; disconnecting removes them.",
  "immaginiDegliEsercizi": "Exercise images",
  "fotoDegliEserciziVengono": "Exercise photos are downloaded, when needed, from the public free-exercise-db collection on GitHub. GitHub receives the phone's IP address and which image is requested, nothing else.",
  "assistenteFacoltativo2": "Assistant (optional)",
  "soloSeAttiviTu": "Only if you turn it on, the assistant sends a summary of your workouts (sessions of the last 4 weeks, feedback, recovery, heart rate zones and bike FTP, plan for the next 14 days) to the service you choose: Anthropic, OpenAI, Google or Ollama on your PC. Name, photo and GPS routes are never sent; age, sex and weight only if you allow it. Before turning it on you can see exactly what is sent. The API key stays encrypted on the phone. For online services their privacy terms and any costs of your subscription apply.",
  "assistenteNellaTuaApp": "Assistant in your app (optional)",
  "seColleghiAppTuo": "If you connect your assistant's app (Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini or others), Avidididadi prepares a message with the same summary described above and passes it to that app only when you tap Share or Copy. From then on the data is in the chat of the chosen service and its rules apply: with a regular subscription chats may be used to train the model, depending on your account settings. Replies you share or paste into the app are read only if they contain the code of your link, and changes to the plan are applied only after you confirm. Until you connect it, Avidididadi doesn't receive text from other apps; when you disconnect it, the code stops being valid.",
  "widgetSullaSchermataHome": "Home screen widget",
  "seAggiungiWidgetSeduta": "If you add the widget, today's session and the week are visible on the home screen, so also to anyone who sees the unlocked phone.",
  "doveRestanoDati": "Where the data stays",
  "nellaCartellaPrivataDell": "In the app's private folder on the phone, which other apps can't access. It doesn't go into Android's automatic backup to Google or the transfer to a new phone: to move it use the app's backup.",
  "fileBackupCreiContiene": "The backup file you create contains all the app data, including health data, photos and GPS routes (not the API key). You save it where you choose: keep it somewhere safe and don't share it. If you turn on automatic backup, the app writes the same file by itself in the folder you chose and keeps the last 5; other apps that read that folder can see it.",
  "permessiTelefono": "Phone permissions",
  "healthConnectLetturaDei": "Health Connect (reading the data listed above), precise location (only during running, walking and cycling), nearby devices (only for the heart rate sensor), physical activity (only for steps while running and walking), internet (maps, images, assistant, updates), install apps (only for app updates, which you confirm each time), notifications (only the one for the workout in progress, with time and data, visible even on the lock screen). You can deny each of these permissions: the app keeps working without the part that needs it.",
  "comeRevocareOCancellare": "How to revoke or delete",
  "healthConnectImpostazioniHealth": "Health Connect: Health Connect settings → App permissions → Avidididadi, or from Profile with \"Review permissions\". Location, nearby devices and physical activity: Android settings → Apps → Avidididadi → Permissions. Heart rate sensor: \"Forget\" in the heart rate sheet, during the workout. Assistant: turn it off and delete the key on the Coach page. To delete everything: Android settings → Apps → Avidididadi → Storage → Clear data, or uninstall the app. The data in Health Connect stays there, because it belongs to the apps that wrote it.",
  "modifiche": "Changes",
  "seQuestaInformativaCambia": "If this policy changes, the app tells you when you open it and asks you to accept it again.",
  "cosAvidididadi": "What Avidididadi is",
  "appPersonalePianificareSeguire": "A personal app to plan and follow strength, running, swimming, cycling and mobility workouts, and to see history and progress. By using it you accept these terms and the privacy policy.",
  "pianiCarichiZoneFrequenza": "Plans, loads, heart rate zones, recovery assessment and the assistant's answers are automatic estimates for information only. They are not a diagnosis or medical advice and don't replace a doctor, physiotherapist or coach. Before starting a training program, especially if you have health problems, are pregnant or haven't trained in a while, ask a doctor. If you feel pain, dizziness, unusual shortness of breath or chest pain, stop and seek help.",
  "allenatiSicurezza": "Train safely",
  "tiAlleniSottoTua": "You train at your own risk: choose loads and paces that suit you, use equipment in good condition and follow the traffic rules. While running, walking or cycling don't look at the phone while moving in traffic.",
  "precisioneDeiDati": "Data accuracy",
  "gpsDistanzeRitmoPassi": "GPS, distances, pace, steps and data read from Health Connect may contain errors (for example between tall buildings or under trees). Calculations and charts depend on this data and how complete it is.",
  "serviziTerzi": "Third-party services",
  "alcuneFunzioniUsanoServizi": "Some features use other parties' services: Health Connect and the apps that write to it (e.g. Garmin Connect), OpenFreeMap and OpenStreetMap for maps, GitHub for exercise images and app updates and, if you turn it on, the artificial intelligence service you choose. These services have their own terms and may change or be unavailable. The API key and the costs of the artificial intelligence service are your responsibility.",
  "tuoiDati": "Your data",
  "datiRestanoSulTuo": "The data stays on your phone and you're responsible for it: make regular backups and keep the file somewhere safe. If you uninstall the app without a backup the data is lost.",
  "nessunaGaranzia": "No warranty",
  "appFornitaCosiCom": "The app is provided as is, with no guarantee that it will work continuously or without errors. To the extent permitted by law, its developer is not liable for damage arising from use of the app, from incorrect data or from data loss.",
  "questiTerminiPossonoEssere": "These terms may be updated. If they change, the app tells you when you open it and asks you to accept them again before continuing.",
