  "webhookComeFunziona": "How it works",
  "webhookComeFunzionaTesto": "Each message is a POST request with a JSON body. If it does not arrive (no network, server down) it stays in a queue and the app retries after 1, 5 and 15 minutes, then every hour, even with the app closed as soon as the network is back: at most 10 times or 7 days. 4xx errors (wrong address or key) are not retried. Format and examples in docs/WEBHOOK.md, in the app's GitHub repository.",
  "webhookFacoltativo": "Webhook (optional)",
  "webhookPrivacy": "Only if you turn on the webhook and enter an https address, the app sends to that address, chosen and run by you, the data of the events you tick: completed workouts (date, times, sport, name, duration, distance, heart rate, power, cadence, steps, calories, RPE, notes, exercises with sets and kg), planned sessions and records. No name, photo, body measurements or GPS routes. The address and secret key stay encrypted on the phone and are not in the backup. The receiver is the service you chose, with its own privacy terms. Turning it off stops all sending and empties the queue.",
